# Bronze, Release 11 / serial 060503, played to the winning ending:
# "*** You have restored the King and freed his servants ***"
#
# Fenced partway down, so an ordinary replay covers the opening and
# stops. The reason, and how to lift it, are written at the fence.
#
# The command stream is adapted from David A. Wheeler's Release 12
# transcript (https://dwheeler.com/bronze/bronze-transcript.html).
# Release 12 survives publicly only as a Glulx build, so that session
# was adapted to the canonical r11 z-code. Three classes of change
# were needed, annotated where they occur:
#
#   1. r11's hint engine asks "Shall I go on?" where r12's did not;
#      each such question gets a "no".
#   2. r11 asks disambiguation questions that r12 resolved silently;
#      each gets the full noun phrase as an answer.
#   3. r12's "go to ivory door" mis-navigated to the drawbridge, and
#      the transcript spends five commands walking back. r11 navigates
#      correctly, so the detour is dropped where noted.
#
# Also: the transcript's lone "walk" is "n" here, and the opening YES
# answers r11's introductory question. Response-diffing the full
# replay against the transcript leaves six divergences, all cosmetic
# (r11 parses "x books"/"x bells" as plurals; two commands both
# releases refuse in different words; one flavor difference on "ring
# gong"). Final tally: 54 of 55 rooms searched, the win banner, and
# the post-win prompt answered with quit.

